.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
This is a collections of short routines that are used with libwget and/or Wget code\&. They may be useful to other developers that is why they are exported\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "size_t wget_strlcpy (char * dst, const char * src, size_t size)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdst\fP Output string buffer 
.br
\fIsrc\fP Input string 
.br
\fIsize\fP Size of \fRdst\fP 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Length of \fRsrc\fP 
.RE
.PP
Copy string \fRsrc\fP into \fRdst\fP with overflow checking\&.

.PP
This is the same as snprintf(dst,size,"%s",src) but faster and more elegant\&.

.PP
If \fRsrc\fP is NULL, the return value is 0 and nothing is written\&. If \\ dst is NULL, the return value is the length of \fRsrc\fP and nothing is written\&. 
.SS "ssize_t wget_strscpy (char * dst, const char * src, size_t size)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdst\fP Output string buffer 
.br
\fIsrc\fP Input string 
.br
\fIsize\fP Size of \fRdst\fP 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Number of copied bytes (excluding trailing 0) or -1 when \fRsrc\fP doesn't fit into \fRdst\fP 
.RE
.PP
Copy string \fRsrc\fP into \fRdst\fP with overflow checking\&.

.PP
If either \fRdst\fP is NULL or \fRsize\fP is 0, the return value is -1 and nothing is written\&. If \fRsrc\fP is NULL and size is 0, the return value is -1\&. If \fRsrc\fP is NULL and size is >0, the return value is 0 and \fRdst\fP is an empty string\&.

.PP
Else the return value is the number of bytes copied to \fRdst\fP excluding the terminating 0\&. 
.SS "int wget_strcmp (const char * s1, const char * s2)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIs1\fP String 
.br
\fIs2\fP String 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
0 if both \fRs1\fP and \fRs2\fP are NULL
.br
 -1 if \fRs1\fP is NULL and \fRs2\fP is not NULL
.br
 1 if \fRs1\fP is not NULL and \fRs2\fP is NULL else it returns strcmp(\fRs1\fP, \fRs2\fP)
.RE
.PP
This functions compares \fRs1\fP and \fRs2\fP in the same way as strcmp() does, except that it also handles NULL values\&. 
